Subject: Shut down the ROS context on component-container early returns

Applies to: RCR rclcpp_components 32.0.3-1.rcr.0,
src/component_container.cpp.

Observed failure: component_container --help prints usage then segfaults,
both in the build tree and an extracted runtime. GDB reaches
spdlog::details::registry::drop from rcl_logging_external_shutdown,
rclcpp::Context::shutdown and the default-context destructor at process exit.

Rationale and scope: the help and invalid-executor paths return after
rclcpp::init without the shutdown performed by the normal execution path.
Shut down explicitly before returning, while logging globals are still alive.
Preserve help/error output and exit statuses; do not change executor behavior.

Verification: //third_party/rclcpp_components:early_exit_test passes all three
help/invalid-executor subcases, returning 0/1/1 without a signal. The complete
existing SDK suite also passes: seven C++ cases and three benchmark operations,
with Cyclone DDS, --config=runtime --config=no-agnocast and ROS_DOMAIN_ID=118.
The consuming distribution has a separate extracted CLI gate.

Upstream: rolling's component_container.cpp retrieved 2026-11-23 retains
these early returns without shutdown. No matching fix association is recorded.
https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/blob/rolling/rclcpp_components/src/component_container.cpp

--- a/src/component_container.cpp
+++ b/src/component_container.cpp
@@ -135,0 +136 @@
+    rclcpp::shutdown();
@@ -141,0 +143 @@
+    rclcpp::shutdown();
